# Plugin scripts

Plain Node CommonJS. No `package.json`, no build, no TypeScript.

- `require()`, not ESM `import`.
- New entry script: `#!/usr/bin/env node`; `require('./lib/settings').takeEditorFlagOrExit(process.argv)` before anything reads `process.argv`; `require('./lib/access-guard').ensureInternalUser()` (`check-setup.js` and `setup-secrets.js` skip it because they report the account check themselves).
- Resolve plugin-internal paths with `__dirname` and the contexts folder and the editor with `lib/paths.js`. Never rebuild them from `process.argv[1]`.
- Read config through `lib/settings.js` → `~/.make-custom-app-skill-secrets`. Never print token values to logs or stdout.
- Tests: `node --test "shared/scripts/lib/__tests__/*.test.js"` (`node:test`, not the mcp-server vitest suite). Keep the quotes so Node expands the glob in any shell.
- Entry script and logic: a script that needs tests keeps its I/O (network, files, exit codes) in `scripts/<name>.js` and its decisions as pure functions in `scripts/lib/<name>-logic.js`, with a different file name. Tests: `lib/__tests__/<name>-logic.test.js` for the logic, `lib/__tests__/<name>.test.js` for the script against a mock server (example: `run-component.js`).
- Adding or renaming a script: update the Scripts table of `README.md` (CI compares it with `shared/scripts/*.js`) and the scripts line of `shared/index.md`.
